            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p><strong>How Athletes Think About Air Wellness</strong></p><p>Elite athletes rely on teams of experts — trainers, physical therapists, nutritionists — all working toward one goal: peak performance. Increasingly, environmental wellness, including air wellness, is becoming part of that conversation.</p><p>Athletes like Jessica Pegula  understand that performance isn’t just about what you put into your body — it’s also about what surrounds you.</p><p><strong>The Athlete Perspective on Air Wellness</strong></p><p>Athletes are uniquely tuned into their bodies. They notice small changes in breathing, recovery, and energy that others might overlook. That awareness often leads them to prioritize:</p><ul><li>Cleaner training environments</li><li>Better sleep conditions</li><li>Reduced exposure to airborne irritants</li></ul><p>Clean, fresh indoor air can help minimize stress on the respiratory system, supporting endurance, recovery, and overall comfort.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
